{
  "configuration_id": "config_019",
  "reason": "The RNA encoder axis has only been tested with scgpt (~0.51-0.54) and scvi_n200 (~0.65-0.72); pca_n2000 remains completely untested, leaving a large uncertainty about whether a simple linear dimensionality reduction can approach the performance of a learned generative representation. Config_019 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is a controlled comparison that holds model setting, profile setting, and aggregation constant while varying only the RNA encoder, enabling a direct three-way contrast with config_018 (scgpt, 0.530) and config_005 (scvi_n200, 0.650). This isolates the representation effect cleanly. If pca_n2000 approaches scvi_n200, it suggests the learned representation is not the critical factor and a cheaper encoder suffices; if it falls near scgpt, it confirms that a learned generative model is essential. Under a limited budget, resolving this fundamental question about representation quality is more informative than marginal tweaks to fusion or aggregation in an already well-characterized scvi_n200 regime."
}

